.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead init" 1  "bead init " 
.SH NAME
bead init \- Initialize a new workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead init\fR [\fB\-\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initialize a new bead workspace in the current directory.
.PP
Creates a .beads directory with SQLite database and configuration.
Repeated initialization with the same prefix is safe and deterministic.
The workspace prefix is used as the default prefix for generated bead IDs.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead init                          # Use default prefix \*(Aqbead\*(Aq
  bead init \-\-prefix myteam          # Use custom prefix \*(Aqmyteam\*(Aq
  bead init \-\-prefix taskforce       # Use custom prefix \*(Aqtaskforce\*(Aq
.PP
The workspace must be initialized before creating or managing issues.
Once initialized, all bead commands will operate on this workspace.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR=\fIPREFIX\fR [default: bead]
Custom prefix for bead IDs (default: bead)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
